{:edb/db-before-t 1225 :edb/db-after-t 1226 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534538 50 #inst "2026-10-07T21:18:41.073Z" 13194139534538 true] [17592186115205 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293766 13194139534538 true] [17592186115205 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293773 13194139534538 true] [17592186115206 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293760 13194139534538 true] [17592186115206 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293763 13194139534538 true] [17592186115613 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534538 true] [17592186115613 1100 "A quadratic equation in the variable $x$ with real coefficients has a root $x =-\\textrm{i}$. Given that the coefficient of $x^{2}$ in the equation is $-2$, find the equation." 13194139534538 false] [17592186115613 1100 "A quadratic equation in the variable $x$ with real coefficients has a root $x=-\\text{i}.$ Given that the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ in the equation is $-2$, find the equation." 13194139534538 true] [17592186115613 1145 "Since the quadratic equation has real coefficients and  $x=-\\text{i}$ is a root, its conjugate  $x=\\text{i}$ must also be a root. Therefore, using the zero product property, we can write a quadratic equation with the required roots as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-\\text{i})(x+\\text{i})=0\n$$\n\nMultiplying out the parentheses and simplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-(\\text{i})^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(-1) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation has roots $x=\\pm \\text{i},$ but the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ is not $-2.$ Therefore, to find the desired equation, we multiply the equation above by $-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2({x}^{2}+1) & =0 \\\\ -2{x}^{2}-2 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293760 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293761 13194139534538 true] [17592186293760 1089 "q-281349" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293760 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534538 true] [17592186293760 1100 "A quadratic equation with real coefficients has a complex root $x=\\sqrt{2}+3\\text{i}.$ Given that the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ in the equation is $1,$ find the equation. Write your answer in the form $a{x}^{2}+bx+c=0,$ where $a,$ $b,$ and $c$ are real constants.\n\n{{field-1}}$=0$" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293760 1113 #uuid "4773acbb-4d68-5273-91de-779cf2e7db02" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293760 1145 "Since the quadratic equation has real coefficients and $x=\\sqrt{2}+3\\text{i}$ is a root, we know that its complex conjugate $x=\\sqrt{2}-3\\text{i}$ is also a root. Therefore, using the zero product property, we can write a quadratic equation with the required roots as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-(\\sqrt{2}+3\\text{i}))(x-(\\sqrt{2}-3\\text{i}))=0\n$$\n\nBy expanding the parentheses, we can write the equation in standard form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-x(\\sqrt{2}+3\\text{i})-x(\\sqrt{2}-3\\text{i})+(\\sqrt{2}+3\\text{i})(\\sqrt{2}-3\\text{i}) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-\\sqrt{2}x-\\cancel{3x\\text{i}}-\\sqrt{2}x+\\cancel{3x\\text{i}}+2-9{\\text{i}}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\sqrt{2}\\,x+2+9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\sqrt{2}\\,x+11 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293761 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293762 13194139534538 true] [17592186293761 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534538 true] [17592186293761 1041 "field-1" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293761 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293762 13194139534538 true] [17592186293761 1110 #uuid "0d243446-722f-54af-b066-db2a2530ec83" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293762 1034 "x^2-2\\sqrt{2}x+11" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293762 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534538 true] [17592186293762 1111 #uuid "ba1033dd-87e2-53bc-ac90-06f691500078" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293763 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293764 13194139534538 true] [17592186293763 1089 "q-281362" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293763 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534538 true] [17592186293763 1100 "A quadratic equation in the variable $x$ with real coefficients has a root $x=2+\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}.$ Given that the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ in the equation is $5,$ find the equation. Write your answer in the form $a{x}^{2}+bx+c=0,$ where $a,$ $b,$ and $c$ are real constants.\n\n{{field-1}}$=0$" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293763 1113 #uuid "42d734ce-bfbe-599a-be22-d761336041fc" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293763 1145 "Since the quadratic equation has real coefficients and $x=2+\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}$ is a root, its conjugate $x=2-\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}$ must also be a root. Therefore, using the zero product property, we can write a quadratic equation with the required roots as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-(2+\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}))(x-(2-\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}))=0\n$$\n\nBy expanding the parentheses, we can write the equation in standard form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-x(2+\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i})-x(2-\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i})+(2+\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i})(2-\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x-\\cancel{x\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}}-2x+\\cancel{x\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}}+4-3{\\text{i}}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+4+3 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+7 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation has roots $x=2\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i},$ but the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ is not $5.$ Therefore, to find the desired equation, we multiply the equation above by $5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5({x}^{2}-4x+7) & =0 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}-20x+35 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293765 13194139534538 true] [17592186293764 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534538 true] [17592186293764 1041 "field-1" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293764 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293765 13194139534538 true] [17592186293764 1110 #uuid "ce3ef4f6-1742-5d49-8b20-c2b99adb9979" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293765 1034 "5x^2-20x+35" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293765 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534538 true] [17592186293765 1111 #uuid "af9a87dc-d1fb-5866-96a8-3e45c6e4e2a4" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293766 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293767 13194139534538 true] [17592186293766 1089 "q-28520" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293766 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534538 true] [17592186293766 1100 "A quadratic equation in the variable $x$ with real coefficients has a root $x=-3\\text{i}.$ Given that the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ in the equation is $-5$, find the equation." 13194139534538 true] [17592186293766 1113 #uuid "86f6b095-6a7b-53c1-a17a-97b2e5ee73eb" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293766 1145 "Since the quadratic equation has real coefficients and  $x=-3\\text{i}$ is a root, its conjugate  $x=3\\text{i}$ must also be a root. Therefore, using the zero product property, we can write a quadratic equation with the required roots as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i})=0\n$$\n\nMultiplying out the parentheses and simplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-9(-1) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+9 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation has roots $x=\\pm 3\\text{i},$ but the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ is not $-5.$ Therefore, to find the desired equation, we multiply the equation above by $-5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5({x}^{2}+9) & =0 \\\\ -5{x}^{2}-45 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293767 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293768 13194139534538 true] [17592186293767 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293769 13194139534538 true] [17592186293767 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293770 13194139534538 true] [17592186293767 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293771 13194139534538 true] [17592186293767 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293772 13194139534538 true] [17592186293767 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534538 true] [17592186293767 1041 "selection" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293767 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293771 13194139534538 true] [17592186293767 1110 #uuid "04e8d433-e940-54f7-bfae-76a9b882a830" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293768 1034 "5{x}^{2}-9=0" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293768 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534538 true] [17592186293768 1111 #uuid "fd5a95af-d156-5c01-9ba0-71687eee251d" 13194139534538 true] [17592186293769 1034 "-5{x}^{2}+9=0" 13194139534538 true]